
# Golden reference files must stay byte-exact (gate: cmp) - no EOL normalization
Verilog/sim/golden/** -text
Verilog/runSim/golden/** -text

# Anything a POSIX shell or make actually EXECUTES must stay LF.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so without these rules git rewrites
# these files to CRLF on checkout - and then bash reads the trailing  as part
# of the command and fails with lines like:
#     tests/run_all_tests.sh: line 21: $'': command not found
#
# That is not hypothetical: it broke `make test` outright on 28-AUG-2026, the
# moment a rebase caused git to re-write run_all_tests.sh. The scripts are run
# from WSL while git runs on the Windows side, so this will happen again to
# anyone who touches them without this rule.
*.sh    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.mk    text eol=lf

# configure.py is run as ./configure.py from WSL too; a CRLF shebang line would
# make that fail with "/usr/bin/env: 'python3\r'".
configure.py text eol=lf
# local.mk.example is read by make-syntax readers; keep it like the .mk files.
local.mk.example text eol=lf
